1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,233
It's up! My eye never misses.

2
00:00:02,233 --> 00:00:04,700
Dad, your friend's went up too.

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:09,167
That's luck. Mine is skill.

4
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:13,067
Mine goes up: skill. Yours goes up: luck. Double standard, number one.

5
00:00:13,067 --> 00:00:15,267
I'm… Modapman.

6
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:22,467
Case summary. Weekday afternoon, the local bank. Ticket number 47.

7
00:00:22,467 --> 00:00:25,967
Today's about opening Moragu's account. No stock talk.

8
00:00:25,967 --> 00:00:29,367
Mine goes up, theirs dips a bit. That's fair.

9
00:00:29,367 --> 00:00:30,733
That is not fair.

10
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:32,933
Just three rounds. Round one: when it goes up.

11
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:34,300
What did you look at before buying?

12
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,267
Your dad reads charts.

13
00:00:37,267 --> 00:00:39,300
You bought it because the name sounded cool.

14
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,533
…But I had a feeling. So what~

15
00:00:42,533 --> 00:00:44,467
Double standard, number two.

16
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:47,033
This is called the self-serving bias.

17
00:00:47,033 --> 00:00:48,467
Self… what?

18
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:50,033
Customer number 47.

19
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:51,867
One sec, this is important!

20
00:00:51,867 --> 00:00:55,533
Up means skill, down means "someone rigged it." Everyone says that.

21
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:57,167
Round two: when it goes down.

22
00:00:57,167 --> 00:00:59,000
Huh? Why's it blue? (Blue means down here.)

23
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,733
The market's rigged. Someone's behind this!

24
00:01:01,733 --> 00:01:03,633
That's exactly what the bank lady said.

25
00:01:03,633 --> 00:01:05,733
Dude… mine's completely blue…

26
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:06,900
Told you so~

27
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:10,133
Wait, it's cheap now? Should I buy some?

28
00:01:10,133 --> 00:01:12,433
Honey, your friend is literally crying.

29
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:13,967
Double standard, number three.

30
00:01:13,967 --> 00:01:16,667
The pain of losing outweighs the joy of winning.

31
00:01:16,667 --> 00:01:18,133
So should I buy or not?

32
00:01:18,133 --> 00:01:20,700
I recommend absolutely nothing.

33
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:23,000
Round three: the family group chat.

34
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,200
My cousin posted his gains.

35
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,600
Ugh… my stomach suddenly hurts.

36
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,700
Dad, why does your tummy hurt?

37
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:32,233
Because his cousin went up.

38
00:01:32,233 --> 00:01:35,100
Why post that? He's just bragging.

39
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:39,000
Crop out the blue… This is just sharing info. So what~

40
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,067
Double standard, number four.

41
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:44,833
Your cousin going up doesn't make yours any smaller.

42
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:46,700
The only thing that shrank is your heart.

43
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:47,133
…Huh?

44
00:01:47,933 --> 00:01:50,967
Dad, I got my own bankbook. Mom and I made it.

45
00:01:51,033 --> 00:01:53,667
Are you happy when your friend's goes down?

46
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:56,000
…No. Of course not.

47
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,133
When your friend goes up, his mood goes up too.

48
00:01:59,267 --> 00:02:02,133
…You're right. I should say congrats.

49
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:04,500
Now, let's check my skills again…

50
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,800
…It's all blue?

51
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,300
Our family account is red. I bought those.

52
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:10,800
…When?

53
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,467
While you picked by name, I did my homework.

54
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:18,467
That's not a double standard. Just a wrong answer. The model answer: Mom.

55
00:02:18,467 --> 00:02:21,333
Customer 47's business was handled by your wife.

56
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:22,933
…Classic Modapman.
